dashboard.definition:
{
  "visualizations": {
    "viz_mission": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "# Code-generation agent bounds\n\nThis is a REPLAY workshop. Path A is the ledger you fill before Path B. The packet is not policy.\n\nA code-generation agent's authority must be bounded and evidenced. Identity claim is not authentication. Delegation is not authorization. Approval of a read is not approval of an install. A current credential is not a tool grant. No GitHub credential is used and no external repository is modified.\n",
        "fontColor": "#17202A",
        "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
        "fontSize": "large"
      }
    },
    "viz_debt": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "# Bounded record\n\n- claimed agent: acme-agent-coder-001\n- authentication: SIMULATED AUTHENTICATION RESULT\n- delegated operation: read_repository\n- approved operation: read_repository\n- approval authority: NOT PROVEN\n- credential: sim-cred-coder-001, status CURRENT\n- dependency name: example-lib, not installed\n",
        "fontColor": "#17202A",
        "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
        "fontSize": "large"
      }
    },
    "viz_request": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "# Request\n\nATTACK and RETEST submit `install_dependency`. The delegated and approved operation is `read_repository`.\n\nBASELINE submits `read_repository`.\n\nPull request and deploy stay NOT OPENED or NOT REQUESTED. Write the binding before Path B.\n",
        "fontColor": "#17202A",
        "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
        "fontSize": "large"
      }
    },
    "viz_pathb": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "# Path B — review\n\n- ATTACK: binding MISMATCH, ALLOW only as vulnerable_profile_fail_open:code_agent_scope_not_checked, simulated start, pull request NOT OPENED.\n- RETEST: binding MISMATCH, DENY operation_not_granted, do not infer execution.\n- BASELINE: binding MATCH, ALLOW tool_granted. A read grant is not authority to install, open a pull request, or deploy.\n\nResource impact is NOT PROVEN.\n",
        "fontColor": "#17202A",
        "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
        "fontSize": "large"
      }
    },
    "viz_guide_shell": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "title": "Guided path",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "# Where you are\n\n**checkpoint · Component Provenance → Code Agent Bounds → L9** · Code Agent Bounds · step 28 of 32 · REPLAY\n\n# What you are learning\n\nCode Agent Bounds\n\n# What you do now\n\n1. Follow this workshop's own specimen or question. It does not mint a run.id.\n2. Use the searches already on the later tabs.\n3. Keep simulated, historical, and measured claims in the words this workshop already uses.\n\n# What to investigate\n\nWhat question is this workshop asking, and which claim does the evidence still leave open?\n\n# What a row means\n\nA `decision` value is a control result. `executed=true` on a start or complete event is execution evidence. Those are different events. A decision row does not prove a handler ran. An execution row does not prove a downstream resource changed.\n\n# What this does not prove\n\nA control decision is not execution. Execution is not a measured downstream resource change. An empty table is not DENY. HEC HTTP 200 is not this table. One RETEST is not universal protection. Progress on Your path is not a security verdict.\n\n# States you may see\n\n**NO RUN.ID** — the box is empty. Launch or select a run, then enter its run.id.\n\n**NO INDEXED RESULTS YET** — zero rows after a real id. Indexing can lag. This is not DENY.\n\n**RUN DENIED** — a control event whose decision is DENY. That is a security result. An empty table is not this state.\n\n**RUN FAILED**, **BACKEND UNAVAILABLE**, and **RUN TIMED OUT** are launcher states. They are not DENY and they are not an empty table.\n\n**NO MATCHING EVIDENCE** — Splunk returned no row for this id. Do not invent the reason.\n\n# SPL used\n\nThis workshop does not add a new run.id search on this tab.\n\nNo new run.id search is added on this tab.\n\n# Conclude\n\nWrite one sentence: what the control decided, and whether a separate event shows execution. Then say one thing the evidence does not prove.\n\n# Next\n\n[Change Bounds](/app/agentsec/ws_lab_change_bounds)\n\nRecord navigation on [Your path](/app/agentsec/learner_path). Opening this page does not mark the workshop investigated.\n",
        "fontSize": "large",
        "fontColor": "#17202A"
      }
    },
    "viz_flow_diagram": {
      "type": "splunk.image",
      "title": "Architecture flow",
      "description": "A read grant is not an install. No GitHub credential is used.",
      "options": {
        "src": "/en-US/static/app/agentsec/flows/flow-lab-code-agent-bounds.svg",
        "preserveAspectRatio": true
      }
    }
  },
  "dataSources": {},
  "defaults": {
    "visualizations": {
      "splunk.table": {
        "options": {
          "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
          "headerBackgroundColor": "#0B1F33",
          "headerTextColor": "#FFFFFF"
        }
      },
      "splunk.markdown": {
        "options": {
          "fontColor": "#17202A",
          "fontSize": "large"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "inputs": {},
  "layout": {
    "type": "grid",
    "options": {
      "submitButton": false,
      "submitOnDashboardLoad": true,
      "showTitleAndDescription": true
    },
    "tabs": {
